cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DIRT in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DIRT — Discrete-element Interaction-Resolved Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  DIRT is a Discrete Element Method (DEM) physics engine built on the
  GRASS → SOIL → DIRT simulation stack. It resolves every inter-particle
  contact individually, adding granular physics — Hertz–Mindlin contact,
  rotational dynamics, parallel bonds, walls, multisphere clumps, heat
  conduction, and contact analysis — on top of the method-agnostic SOIL
  particle substrate.
type: software
authors:
